///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's SlaughterHordeContainModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see SlaughterHordeContain


/// \class CitadelSlaughterHordeContain
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Contain module registered as "CitadelSlaughterHordeContain": a
///        SlaughterHordeContain with "ring entry" fields.
///
/// It accepts every field of its SlaughterHordeContain chain plus four of
/// its own, all about a "ring entry": a status, upgrades, objects to
/// destroy and an FX list. That presumably refers to the One Ring entering
/// the container, but the code that reads these fields is not described
/// here. CitadelSlaughterHordeContain::xfer transfers its own version,
/// then SlaughterHordeContain's block, then an object id only when the
/// version (on load, the one read from the stream) is 2 or later, so a
/// version-1 record loads without it (\ref grp_w3_module_xfer).
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields (CitadelSlaughterHordeContainModuleData), read from the
/// retail table: \c StatusForRingEntry (object status bits),
/// \c UpgradeForRingEntry (text list), \c ObjectToDestroyForRingEntry
/// (object filter) and \c FXForRingEntry (FX list).
///
/// \see CitadelSlaughterHordeContain::friend_newModuleInstance

/// \fn Module *CitadelSlaughterHordeContain::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "CitadelSlaughterHordeContain":
///        creates the container for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's CitadelSlaughterHordeContainModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see CitadelSlaughterHordeContain


/// \class ProductionQueueHordeContain
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Contain module registered as "ProductionQueueHordeContain": a
///        HordeGarrisonContain with a list of destination entries.
///
/// It accepts every field of its HordeGarrisonContain chain plus one of
/// its own, \c DestinationTemplate, read by a dedicated parser: each
/// \c DestinationTemplate line adds one entry to a list, a name followed
/// by an object filter. How the container uses those entries, and how it
/// relates to production queues, is not described here.
///
/// \see ProductionQueueHordeContain::friend_newModuleInstance

/// \fn Module *ProductionQueueHordeContain::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "ProductionQueueHordeContain":
///        creates the container for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's ProductionQueueHordeContainModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see ProductionQueueHordeContain


/// \class ActiveBody
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Body module registered as "ActiveBody": the standard body with
///        health and damage states, and the base of the other body modules
///        in this group.
///
/// Zero Hour: ActiveBody keeps the object's current and maximum health,
/// passes incoming damage through the object's armor and moves the body
/// between damage states. In BFME 2 the body classes in this group derive
/// from it: OathbreakerBody, RespawnBody, DetachableRiderBody,
/// SymbioticStructuresBody and PorcupineFormationBodyModule directly, and
/// DelayedDeathBody and FreeLifeBody through RespawnBody. HighlanderBody,
/// ImmortalBody and StructureBody, which are not documented here, also
/// derive from it. Its data class is the start of every body field table
/// in this group. Its instance factory is not documented here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Fields (ActiveBodyModuleData), read from the retail table:
/// \c MaxHealth, \c MaxHealthDamaged, \c MaxHealthReallyDamaged and
/// \c InitialHealth (reals); \c RecoveryTime,
/// \c EnteringDamagedTransitionTime and
/// \c EnteringReallyDamagedTransitionTime (durations); \c DodgePercent
/// (percent); \c GrabObject (text), \c GrabFX (FX list), \c GrabDamage
/// (real) and \c GrabOffset (2D coordinate); \c UseDefaultDamageSettings
/// (boolean); \c DamageCreationList (dedicated parser); \c HealingBuffFx (FX
/// list); \c DamagedAttributeModifier and \c ReallyDamagedAttributeModifier
/// (text); \c CheerRadius (real); \c RemoveUpgradesOnDeath and
/// \c BurningDeathBehavior (booleans); \c BurningDeathFX (FX list). Zero
/// Hour's table has \c MaxHealth, \c InitialHealth and three subdual-damage
/// fields; the subdual fields are not in BFME 2's table.
///
/// \see ActiveBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class ActiveBodyModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for ActiveBody, HighlanderBody, ImmortalBody and
///        OathbreakerBody, and the base of the other body data classes here.
///
/// Built once per module line by ActiveBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData
/// and shared by every object of the template.

/// \fn ModuleData *ActiveBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "ActiveBody", "HighlanderBody",
///        "ImmortalBody" and "OathbreakerBody": creates the body data and
///        parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through any of the four
/// registrations, so a module line naming one of those bodies accepts the
/// ActiveBody fields and nothing else. The group page describes the shared
/// pattern.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see ActiveBody, OathbreakerBody


/// \class OathbreakerBody
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Body module registered as "OathbreakerBody": an ActiveBody
///        subclass that reads exactly the ActiveBody fields.
///
/// Its registration uses ActiveBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData, so it
/// has no INI fields of its own. Its constructor adds nothing to
/// ActiveBody's; what the class does differently from ActiveBody is not
/// described here.
///
/// \see OathbreakerBody::friend_newModuleInstance

/// \fn Module *OathbreakerBody::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "OathbreakerBody": creates the
///        body for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's ActiveBodyModuleData for this module
///                    line.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see ActiveBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData


/// \class RespawnBody
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Body module registered as "RespawnBody": an ActiveBody with
///        respawn settings, and the base of DelayedDeathBody and
///        FreeLifeBody in this group.
///
/// It accepts every ActiveBody field plus two of its own. Their names
/// suggest a body whose object can respawn unless it was killed by an
/// object passing \c PermanentlyKilledByFilter; the respawn code is not
/// described here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields (RespawnBodyModuleData), read from the retail table:
/// \c PermanentlyKilledByFilter (object filter) and \c CanRespawn
/// (boolean).
///
/// \see RespawnBody::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      RespawnBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class RespawnBodyModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for RespawnBody: the ActiveBody fields plus the
///        respawn fields.
///
/// Built once per module line by RespawnBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData.
/// In this group, DelayedDeathBodyModuleData and FreeLifeBodyModuleData
/// derive from it.

/// \fn Module *RespawnBody::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "RespawnBody": creates the body
///        for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's RespawnBodyModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see RespawnBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *RespawnBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "RespawnBody": creates the module
///        data and parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration.
/// The group page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see RespawnBody::friend_newModuleInstance


/// \class DelayedDeathBody
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Body module registered as "DelayedDeathBody": a RespawnBody with
///        delayed-death settings.
///
/// It accepts every ActiveBody and RespawnBody field plus five of its own.
/// Their names suggest that the object's death is delayed by a time, that
/// it can stay immortal until then, and that the behaviour can require an
/// upgrade; the code that does so is not described here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields (DelayedDeathBodyModuleData), read from the retail table:
/// \c DelayedDeathTime (duration), \c ImmortalUntilDeathTime and
/// \c DoHealthCheck (booleans), \c InvulnerableFX (FX list) and
/// \c DelayedDeathPrerequisiteUpgrade (an upgrade, read by
/// INI::parseUpgradeTemplate).
///
/// \see DelayedDeathBody::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      DelayedDeathBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class DelayedDeathBodyModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for DelayedDeathBody: the RespawnBody fields plus the
///        delayed-death fields.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// DelayedDeathBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData.

/// \fn Module *DelayedDeathBody::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "DelayedDeathBody": creates the
///        body for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's DelayedDeathBodyModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see DelayedDeathBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *DelayedDeathBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "DelayedDeathBody": creates the module
///        data and parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration.
/// The group page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see DelayedDeathBody::friend_newModuleInstance


/// \class FreeLifeBody
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Body module registered as "FreeLifeBody": a RespawnBody with
///        "free life" settings.
///
/// It accepts every ActiveBody and RespawnBody field plus five of its own.
/// Their names suggest a one-off reprieve: a health percentage and a time,
/// optional invincibility, an animation, and a required upgrade. The code
/// that grants it is not described here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields (FreeLifeBodyModuleData), read from the retail table:
/// \c FreeLifeHealthPercent (percent), \c FreeLifeTime (duration),
/// \c FreeLifeInvincible (boolean), \c FreeLifePrerequisiteUpgrade (an
/// upgrade, read by INI::parseUpgradeTemplate) and
/// \c FreeLifeAnimAndDuration (an animation with a duration, read by the
/// same parser as the upgrade modules' \c CustomAnimAndDuration).
