/// \class DetachableRiderBody
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Body module registered as "DetachableRiderBody": an ActiveBody
///        that also carries an upgrade trigger, with fields about a rider.
///
/// The class adds an UpgradeMux part to ActiveBody, so besides the
/// ActiveBody fields its INI block accepts the shared upgrade fields that
/// upgrade modules use (\c TriggeredBy, \c ConflictsWith and the rest,
/// read from the same retail table; \ref grp_w1021_upgrade_module_factories
/// lists them) and three fields of its own. When \c StartsActive is set,
/// the constructor calls UpgradeMux::giveSelfUpgrade. Zero Hour: that
/// function plays the upgrade's FX, processes removals and runs the
/// upgrade through three virtual calls, then marks the upgrade executed
/// with an inline setter. BFME 2's body differs: it makes four virtual
/// calls, the last passing true. If those calls follow Zero Hour's order,
/// the upgrade part starts out applied; this page does not confirm what
/// each call does. Read with Zero Hour's bit values, its
/// registration does not carry the upgrade interface bit. The field names
/// suggest a rider that can die or be lost while the body lives on; what
/// the upgrade does to the body is not described here.
///
/// \par Modding
/// Own fields (DetachableRiderBodyModuleData), read from the retail table:
/// \c HealthPercentageWhenRiderDies (percent), \c StartsActive (boolean)
/// and \c RiderlessDeathChance (percent).
///
/// \see DetachableRiderBody::friend_newModuleInstance,
///      DetachableRiderBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \class DetachableRiderBodyModuleData
/// \ingroup grp_w1022_contain_body_module_factories
/// \brief Module data for DetachableRiderBody: the ActiveBody fields, the
///        shared upgrade fields and the rider fields.
///
/// Built once per module line by
/// DetachableRiderBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData.

/// \fn Module *DetachableRiderBody::friend_newModuleInstance(Thing *thing, const ModuleData *moduleData)
/// \brief Instance factory registered for "DetachableRiderBody": creates the
///        body for one object.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModule calls it through the registration. The group
/// page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param thing       The object being built; the module keeps it as its
///                    owner.
/// \param moduleData  The template's DetachableRiderBodyModuleData.
/// \return The new module as the Module base the factory stores, or null
///         when the allocation fails.
/// \see DetachableRiderBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData

/// \fn ModuleData *DetachableRiderBodyModuleData::friend_newModuleData(INI *ini)
/// \brief Data factory registered for "DetachableRiderBody": creates the
///        module data and parses the module's INI block into it.
///
/// ModuleFactory::newModuleDataFromINI calls it through the registration.
/// The group page describes the shared pattern.
///
/// \param ini  The reader positioned on the module's block, or null to
///             keep the constructor defaults.
/// \return The new module data as the ModuleData base the factory stores.
/// \see DetachableRiderBody::friend_newModuleInstance


